    "md5": "b2d5edc9fa54fb077f6f855f5c3012f5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1316,
    "chunk_text": "Rumesh Tharanga takes on world\u2019s best in Budapest tonight\n\nColombo, Sep. 13 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lankan javelin thrower Rumesh Tharanga is set to compete in the men\u2019s javelin throw at the World Athletics Ultimate Championship in Budapest, Hungary, today (13), with the event scheduled to begin at 9.40 p.m. Sri Lanka time.\n\nTharanga enters the competition as the world\u2019s leading javelin thrower this season, having recorded a best throw of 92.62 metres. He also recently secured the Diamond League javelin title.\n\nGermany\u2019s Julian Weber is expected to pose one of the strongest challenges to Tharanga. Weber recently set a championship record of 90.40 metres at the European Athletics Championships.\n\nOlympic champion Arshad Nadeem of Pakistan, Grenada\u2019s Anderson Peters and Trinidad and Tobago\u2019s Keshorn Walcott are among the other leading javelin throwers competing in the event.\n\nThe prestigious championship, which began on September 11, brings together athletes who have achieved major success at the Olympics, World Championships and leading international circuits, including the Diamond League. The competition concludes today.\n\nThe winner of each event will receive a prize of US$150,000, while cash prizes will be awarded through eighth place, with the eighth-placed athlete receiving US$10,000."
