    "md5": "870f0ad4bf7be3aa196bb2ea6f1a11f7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1650,
    "chunk_text": "KEMCARE at 11: Celebrating a journey of innovation, empowering industry, shaping future\n\nKEMCARE Technologies Ltd. marked its 11th anniversary with a grand celebration held on 4 September at Waters Edge, Battaramulla, bringing together distinguished Government officials, industry leaders, business partners, customers, manufacturers, and key stakeholders from across the country.\n\nThe celebration marked 11 years of KEMCARE\u2019s journey, built on a strong foundation of innovation, quality, trust, and lasting relationships.\n\nSince its inception, KEMCARE has continued to strengthen its presence in Sri Lanka\u2019s rapidly evolving beauty and household cleaning products industry, supporting local manufacturers and creating opportunities for businesses operating within the sector.\n\nThe milestone was celebrated under the leadership of KEMCARE Technologies Director Sumedha Abayarathna, Directress Nayomi Rathnayaka, and KEMCARE Chief Executive Officer Charitha Perera, whose leadership and strategic direction have contributed to the company\u2019s continued growth and development.\n\nA key highlight of the evening was the gathering of prominent Government and industry leaders under one roof, creating a valuable platform for networking, knowledge sharing, and strengthening collaboration between the public and private sectors.\n\nAmong the distinguished guests were Sri Lanka Export Development Board Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe, National Enterprise Development Authority Chairman Lakshman Abeysekara, and Director General of Government Information Harsha Bandara, alongside a strong representation of industry stakeholders."
  },
