    "language": "en",
    "md5": "236a4107fad2a5fe31d436e35bd5b5bd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1915,
    "chunk_text": "They can study geopolitical developments before they become crises. They can examine the economic implications of international agreements. They can develop options for maritime strategy, national security, energy security and food security. They can assess emerging technologies and their implications for national competitiveness. They can bring international experts into domestic policy debates and, equally importantly, provide Sri Lankan policymakers with access to international policy networks.\n\nOne of the things I learned was that the Government had provided approximately seven acres of land, while significant support for the development of the centre had come from the business community in Pune. This is an important lesson for Sri Lanka.\n\nIndia\u2019s business community has increasingly recognised that supporting knowledge institutions is not simply philanthropy. A strong think-tank ecosystem can contribute to a better business environment, stronger economic policy, improved international engagement and greater national competitiveness. The private sector ultimately operates within the policies created by governments. Therefore, businesses have a legitimate interest in supporting institutions that improve the quality of public policy. Sri Lanka\u2019s business community could learn from this model.\n\nOur companies invest heavily in infrastructure, technology, human resources and corporate social responsibility. There is also a strong case for investing in knowledge infrastructure, institutions that examine the country\u2019s future and help develop solutions to complex national challenges. This becomes even more important when we consider the challenges facing Sri Lanka. The country cannot approach maritime affairs, regional connectivity, national security, food security, disaster resilience, financial crime or human trafficking as completely separate issues. They increasingly intersect."
