    "chunk_text": "However, during the North-East monsoon (December to February) and first inter monsoon period (March and April) that usually has few showers in the North Eastern part, will see a dryer than usual situation and people will feel high temperatures.\n\n\u201cThe Department of Meteorology is having regular stakeholder meetings with all stakeholders including with the Water Management Secretariat and the agriculture sector to share the latest forecasts and climate information and discuss the possible implications for water resources\u201d Hendawitharana said.\n\n\u201cPeople should be aware that seasonal forecasts indicate probabilities rather than certainty. Therefore, we need to continue monitoring the evolving conditions and regularly update the forecasts as new information becomes available,\u201d she said.\n\nAccording to the Disaster Management Centre, over 160,000 people in Ampara, Anuradhapura, Badulla, Batticaloa, Matale, Monaragala, Polonnaruwa, and Ratnapura are affected by El Ni\u00f1o.\n\nNational Disaster Relief Services Centre Senior Assistant Secretary Prageeth Danansooriya said distribution of drinking water commenced through the district secretariat and divisional secretariats, while local government authorities are also supporting the program. Over 140,000 people are receiving drinking water in eight districts.\n\n\u201cWe have increased the amount of water given to affected people from six liters per day per person to 50 liters per day per person. We have also introduced a special phone number 0716807807 for anyone who faces difficulty in receiving drinking water to complain. We will then facilitate those areas,\u201d he said.\n\nIn Kadurugaswewa, an extremely rural village, women now depend on what they call a \u2018water hole\u2019, a stagnant stretch of a once-flowing waterway that remains after the rest of the water has dried up, to fetch water in for cleaning and cooking. Under the scorching sun, the women collect water in containers and use wheelbarrows to carry the heavy loads back home."
