    "chunk_text": "The pace at which the project has advanced reflects the strength of the construction planning behind it, as well as the coordinated execution of two specialised engineering teams working in parallel across the site. Prime Construction Ltd., the Group\u2019s in-house construction arm, leads the construction of two towers, while Sanken Lanka Ltd., leads the construction of the other tower.\n\nPrime Lands Residencies PLC Chairperson Sandamini Perera said: \u201cThe completion of the superstructures across all three towers represents another important achievement for the Group and for the wider development of the project.\u201d She noted that maintaining this pace of construction, without compromising on quality, reflected the Group\u2019s consistent commitment to delivering its projects on schedule, adding, \u201cThe trust placed in the Prime brand by buyers is valued at every stage of the project. It represents an investment in which the company will continue to honor with quality engineering and construction excellence as The Colombo Border moves into its next phase.\u201d\n\nRedefining modern condominium living in Sri Lanka, The Colombo Border offers residents an exceptional lifestyle through its strategic location, expansive green spaces, premium amenities, sustainable design, and a strong sense of community. The development has earned the confidence of homeowners and investors alike. With Tower Cosmos now completely sold out with limited two and three BR apartments are available starting from Rs. 48 million upwards, the project reflects The Colombo Border\u2019s outstanding market appeal and long-term investment potential. The Colombo Border presents an ideal opportunity for existing homeowners looking to expand their investment portfolio, as well as new buyers seeking a future-ready home in one of Colombo\u2019s fastest-growing residential destinations."
