    "md5": "2864007c1509f1f8ff1e1ea6f59d79a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1772,
    "chunk_text": "SLPA to launch FDI-backed logistics hub at Colombo Port in three months\n\nSLPA to establish foreign direct investment-backed logistics hub within a free zone at the Port of Colombo in two to three months\n\nCabinet approval for a new committee to address maritime industry concerns expected this week, with active input from NVOCCs\n\nThe Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA) is preparing to launch a comprehensive logistics hub within a free zone at the Port of Colombo over the next two to three months, backed by foreign direct investments (FDI).\n\nThe announcement was made during the 9th Annual General Meeting of the Sri Lanka Association of NVOCC Agents (SLANA), held in Colombo last week.\n\nAddressing the gathering, SLPA Chairman Dr. Parakrama Dissanayake revealed that the upcoming project represents a significant policy shift aimed at transitioning the nation into a true logistics center.\n\n\u201cOver the last 40 years, while handling millions of TEUs, we never fully became a logistics hub because a logistics hub requires establishments outside the Port of Colombo. We never had that,\u201d Dr. Dissanayake stated. \u201cOn the advice of the minister, within the next two to three months, we will be truly launching a logistics hub, ideally in a free zone in the Port of Colombo. So from a policy end, changing altogether, SLPA will be launching this with FDI.\u201d\n\nSpeaking as the Chief Guest, Minister of Ports and Civil Aviation Anura Karunathilaka assured the shipping community that the government is actively responding to industry feedback regarding regulatory frameworks. Acknowledging the concerns raised by the local shipping community, he announced the imminent formation of a new industry committee to evaluate these issues, with cabinet approval expected this week."
