    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe bottom line is that ports, terminal operators, NVOCCs, are at the mercy of these five shipping lines,\u201d he added.\u00a0 Noting that these leading carriers have transformed from simple ship operators into comprehensive supply chain service providers equipped with massive hardware advantages, he urged SLANA members to shift their operational roles.\n\n\u201cSLANA\u2019s role should change from representing NVOCC agents, to supply chain orchestrators enabling Sri Lanka\u2019s next-generation logistics,\u201d he advised.\n\n\u201cPillar number one is resilience. Always have another route,\u201d he advised, referencing how the Sri Lankan tea industry successfully survived past crises by rerouting shipments. He identified digitalisation and sustainability as the second pillar, warning that future cargo shipments to Europe will demand strict accountability for carbon footprints.\n\nFinally, he emphasised human capital and proactive agility as the third pillar. Reminding the industry that people ultimately make or break organizations, he urged proactive policy advocacy and concluded that the future will not belong to the biggest or the cheapest, but to the agile. (NF)"
