    "md5": "e6d439d953dfc2f9e30b68d7fba446a4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1285,
    "chunk_text": "Deputy Solicitor General Janaka Bandara told court that Rajapaksa\u2019s arrest followed a joint investigation by CIABOC and the CID, with help from authorities in Australia, Singapore, France, and the United States. According to court submissions, \u20ac1.45 million had allegedly been paid by Airbus in connection with the transaction. Investigators examined funds originating from a Singapore bank account under \u201cBiz Solution,\u201d owned by Priyanka Niyomali Wijenayake, wife of former CEO Kapila Chandrasena. Funds from that account were transferred to a Singapore account belonging to a company chaired by Nimal Perera.\n\nThese transactions may form an evidentiary chain, but prosecutors must establish a direct, provable connection between the money and the alleged payment to Rajapaksa.\n\nFollowing a change of government, SriLankan Airlines sought to withdraw from some aircraft arrangements, incurring penalties exceeding US$100 million. A high-powered inquiry followed, yet despite recommendations that former executives face prosecution, those investigations did not result in convictions. If corruption occurred, why did it take so long to pursue? If evidence existed, why did it fail to yield convictions? These questions cannot be answered simply by arresting another politician."
