    "chunk_id": "2026-09-14-dailymirrorlk-378d8fe5-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "779c343f29bb9a6f33ce6a30ab8ec4b7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1799,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cWe don\u2019t believe in becoming a power broker\u201d-Dilith Jayaweera, Leader of Sarvajana Balaya\n\n\u201cAs Sarvajana Balaya we believe that we should build a national political narrative\u201d- Dilith Jayaweera, Leader Sarvajana Balaya\n\nBringing 22nd Amendment would be disastrous and would result repercussions which would affect the country\u2019s democracy\n\nJust because I\u2019ve been an effective strategist for others doesn\u2019t necessarily guarantee the same for myself\n\nBrands and personalities or political parties as brands is an evolving process\n\nWe\u2019re confident we can build a brand that is relevant to youth, GenZs, Gen Alpha and the millennials\n\nWe have a programme called hundred new faces. The youth as our next leadership\n\nHow will we create wealth if you are going to keep these 50% of the population as housewives?\n\nIn a recent interview with Daily Mirror, MP Dilith Jayaweera said that Sarvajana Balaya\u2019s vision is to govern rather than act as a political power broker for major political parties. Drawing on his background as an entrepreneur and brand strategist, Jayaweera acknowledged that he isn\u2019t happy about his political campaign. He underscored that fact that lasting support cannot be built on media presence alone though it could attract attention for a short period of time. Instead, he believes that earning public trust through hands-on experience as a long-term challenge; one he believes he will achieve by cultivating strong, youth-led second-tier leadership. The Parliamentarian stated that as a new political party he is happy with the party\u2019s progress. He further said that NPP is governing the country in the most archaic manner and added that bringing 22nd Amendment would be disastrous and would result repercussions which would affect the country\u2019s democracy."
  },
