    "md5": "1c67497a52a7dc9ab0a563e3f969b839",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1791,
    "chunk_text": "But my biggest problem with the NPP is its, central ideology steming from the JVP. And the JVP isn\u2019t a party which believed in modern Economy. They still follow traditional beliefs. We need more than that. So, my submission and my proposition is that, when a political party does not have a progressive core philosophy, it is difficult to adapt to suit the modern world and the global competition. And realise the global economic challenges. So today, what is evident in their governance is that they are not susceptible, and ready. They are instead going in the most archaic manner that you can look at the world today.\n\nQIn your opinion, why is the government campaigning strongly for 22nd Amendment irrespective of the strong opposition from the BASL?\n\nToday if you look at even the socialist countries, they have fully and decisively embraced the entrepreneurial state concept. For example Vietnam and China are supposed to be socialist states. They are promoting entrepreneurship as the nation\u2019s main slogan\n\nQAt present, Sri Lanka relies on funding such as IMF to stabilise the economy. At the same time there have been calls from the west to dismantle laws which penalise sexual minorities. Recently EU had a concern over discrimination of LGBTQ community. In the National Strategic Plan which was published in 2024 by Sarvajana Balaya there is no reference regarding gender. Any particular reason for that? What is your party\u2019s view on quota system for women\u2019s representation?\n\nThe document that we published, is not a traditional manifesto. It is a strategic plan. Here we have summarised our strategy if the country is to be taken to the next level. Our attempt was to establish the thought that the country needs a strategy. This is a document where we discuss strategies."
