    "chunk_text": "Government facing no threat: President\n\nColombo, Sep. 15 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake said yesterday the government is not facing any threat and that the public rallies being held across the country are aimed at building a strong people\u2019s movement to support the country\u2019s development.\n\nSpeaking at a public rally in Kahatagasdigiliya, the President said the responsibility for developing the country lies not only with the government but also with the people.\n\n\u201cThe government must take action to develop the country, while the people too have a major responsibility in this effort. We need to build a strong public movement for this purpose, and that is what we are doing now. There is no threat to the government,\u201d he said.\n\nDissanayake stressed that Sri Lanka\u2019s progress requires economic, political and social transformation.\n\nHe also said the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) government had brought an end to family-based politics, insisting that there should be no room for such a system in the country.\n\n\u201cFor 76 years, several elite families governed this country. We must put an end to family politics. It is an outdated practice, and the NPP has stopped it,\u201d he said.\n\nThe President also called on the public to change their attitudes towards politicians accused of misappropriating public property. He said people should support legal action against those responsible rather than defend them.\n\nReferring to a gathering in Anuradhapura, he said a small group had assembled to defend individuals accused of wrongdoing and had argued that they should not be imprisoned.\n\nDissanayake further claimed that opposition groups were engaged in a do-or-die game to overthrow the government. He said those who got away with wrongdoing under successive governments for decades were now attempting to regain protection."
