    "chunk_size_bytes": 1807,
    "chunk_text": "The offer, if it holds, would cover only about 47 percent of the Rs.2.55 billion in borrowings carried on the group balance sheet as at end-June and a little over half the Rs.2.23 billion at which the group\u2019s property, plant and equipment are stated. The investor has not been identified in the filing.\n\nThe interim accounts for the quarter ended June 30, 2026, released last month, show a group with no operations to defend. Revenue was nil for a second consecutive year, with both hotels shut since November 2022 and the group posted a net loss of Rs.88.5 million or close to Rs.1 million a day, against Rs.190.6 million in the corresponding quarter, which carried a Rs.98.8 million loss on the disposal of assets.\n\nThe finance costs of Rs.55.9 million accounted for the bulk of the deficit and were met almost entirely by Rs.55.4 million in fresh borrowings drawn during the quarter.\n\nThe current liabilities of Rs.2.82 billion now exceed the current assets of Rs.410.4 million by Rs.2.41 billion, widening from the Rs.1.86 billion shortfall the auditors flagged as a going concern risk in March 2024, the last year for which the audited accounts exist.\n\nThe negative net assets deepened to Rs.615.7 million, from Rs.527.2 million three months earlier, while the accumulated losses of Rs.6.35 billion have overtaken the Rs.5.08 billion in stated capital raised since the 2013 listing by Rs.1.27 billion. Cash at the end of the quarter stood at Rs.3.8 million.\n\nHowever, the interim accounts, signed on August 13, record that \u201cno events have occurred since the reporting date which would require any adjustment\u201d and that there has been \u201cno significant change in the nature and value of the contingencies\u201d, despite the bank\u2019s acquisition resolution having been under legal challenge since 2025."
