    "md5": "067ea4a988fafb5f349edd3dd93dfe86",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1587,
    "chunk_text": "The regulator has also taken issue with claims that it said sought to impugn the integrity, impartiality, competence and conduct of the SEC and its officials in discharging their statutory duties and functions under Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Act No. 19 of 2021.\n\nThe SEC has further flagged the amplification of the claims via social media, noting that their wider dissemination had increased their reach and visibility among the public.\n\nIt warned that such statements had the tendency to mislead the investors and public regarding the lawful exercise of the SEC\u2019s regulatory, supervisory, investigative and enforcement powers.\n\nThe development assumes significance, given the critical role of regulatory credibility and investor confidence in the continued development of Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market.\n\nIn a firm response, the SEC has sought the withdrawal of the disputed statements and a public correction expressly acknowledging that the claims were inaccurate, misleading and made without factual basis.\n\nIt has also called for a written and public apology to the SEC, its chairman, members and officers, with the apology to be disseminated through the same media platforms or public forums capable of reaching the original audience.\n\nThe regulator has cautioned that failure to comply within the stipulated period could see it pursue available legal remedies, including the proceedings under the SEC Act and other applicable laws.\n\nThe SEC has expressly reserved its right to seek appropriate relief, including injunctions, damages, compensation and costs."
