    "chunk_size_bytes": 1094,
    "chunk_text": "On terrorism, the summit expressed strong condemnation of any acts of terrorism as criminal and unjustifiable, regardless of motivation. \u201cWe condemn in the strongest terms the terrorist attack in Jammu and Kashmir on 22 April 2025, during which 26 people were killed and many more injured.\n\nOn cross-border payments, the summit acknowledged efforts of the BRICS Payment Task Force toward exploring pragmatic solutions for efficient cross-border payment mechanisms. It welcomed discussions on promoting trade settlements and investments using BRICS local currencies,\u00a0 but he DD pragmatically did not push for aggressive de-dollarisation.\n\nChina and Russia, as permanent members of the UN Security Council, reiterated their support for the aspiration of Brazil and India to play a greater role in the UN, including its Security Council.\n\nBut the DD did not advocate permanent membership of the UNSC for India and Brazil, because the process involves amending the UN Charter which explicitly says that the US, UK, France and China will be the only permanent members in the UNSC with veto power."
