    "md5": "5f90f7bb1d240cb9cb0c662a5e7f3bbd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1769,
    "chunk_text": "El Ni\u00f1o: Disaster drills ordered in landslide-prone districts\n\nColombo, Sep. 15 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka is stepping up disaster preparedness in several landslide-prone districts as authorities anticipate a shift towards wetter weather under the influence of El Ni\u00f1o over the coming months.\n\nThe decision was taken at the fifth meeting of the Special Cabinet Subcommittee and Officials\u2019 Committee appointed to take necessary measures to address the impact of the El Ni\u00f1o climate phenomenon, held at the Presidential Secretariat yesterday (14).\n\nThe meeting was chaired by Minister of Environment Dr. Dhammika Patabendi.\n\nAs the impact of the El Ni\u00f1o climate phenomenon is expected to transition from the prevailing dry conditions to wetter weather over the next two months, the committees discussed measures to prepare for the anticipated changes in weather conditions.\n\nParticular attention was given to the possibility of increased rainfall triggering disasters such as floods and landslides. The committees decided to raise public awareness and conduct disaster preparedness drills to familiarise communities with the appropriate measures to be taken during emergencies.\n\nThe meeting also decided to launch a public awareness programme through electronic and print media.\n\nDiscussions were held on the importance of establishing operational centres at the Divisional Secretariat level to ensure communities are adequately prepared to respond to potential disasters.\n\nMeanwhile, the committees reviewed the progress of relief measures being implemented for people affected by the prevailing El Ni\u00f1o conditions, as well as planned measures to address the anticipated changes in weather.\n\nMirror Missions: El Ni\u00f1o in Sri Lanka, Can You Protect Your Community?"
